In order to be able to remove the file, you would need write (and search)
permissions in the directory.  In fact, even without permission to read
a unix file, you can still rename it or remove it if you have permissions
in the directory.

Above, ralf _does_ have permission to overwrite the file, but might not
be allowed to remove it (directory permissions not shown).  If you
really want to wipe it, try this command

		> /u/nh/bonesM0.T.z

The > is part of the command, not the prompt.  It means "do nothing, directing
all output to the named file".  So you wind up with the same file in the same
directory with the same permissions, but truncated to zero length.

I don't know what nethack will do when it encounters an invalid bones file,
however!

